(ns association.facts
  "Industry rule/history catalog for EK (Elinkeinoelämän keskusliitto,
  Confederation of Finnish Industries), an industry-association-level
  source per ADR-2607141700 (cloud-itonami-compliance-fact-federation),
  aligned to ISIC 9411 (activities of business, employers, and
  professional membership organizations). Finland has real, individually
  verified facts across all three axes: country (cloud-itonami-iso3166-fin
  statute.facts), municipality (cloud-itonami-municipality-fin-helsinki),
  and association (this entry).

  GENERATED by scripts/gen-kotoba-port.cljs from data/datascript-tx.edn,
  together with the Kotoba port in src/association_facts.kotoba. Do not
  hand-edit; add facts to the data file and regenerate.

  Every entry carries the page it came from (:source-article) and the
  verbatim span the claim rests on (:source-quote), and
  `nbb scripts/verify-catalog.cljs --live` fetches each :url and requires
  that span to still be in it. Reachability is not support: a URL that
  returns 200 without the claim reads exactly like one that carries it.
  While this catalog was built, a finlex.fi PDF offered as the English
  Associations Act (503/1989) returned 200 and was the Act on the Finnish
  Red Cross (238/2000). It is not here because the text was read.

  No personal names of office-holders are persisted here.

  An association not in `catalog` has NO spec-basis, full stop; never
  fabricate one."
  (:require [clojure.string]))

